Yes -- this means that I can charge anything I like for bash.  My fee
for distributing a compiled version of bash to you is $100,000.  (Of
course I will include a pointer to the place where the source can be
obtained.)  I can do that without being in violation of the GPL: it
says so.  I am free to redistribute copies, charging a fee for
distribution.  I just can't prevent you from giving it away for free
thereafter.  Neither can I prevent you from just getting the source
yourself and compiling it.

